+RUN_BY_SKILL: vibe-test
+Pipeline-Run: 81d6f968-0843-449a-b3ac-e0fffa47a255
+
+# Vibe test: cd-1 (block A5)
+
+**Tracker:** none
+**Ticket:** TICKET_SKIPPED (none: no tracker declared)
+
+## Target
+
+- Classification: disk spec.
+- Spec file: `.context/proposals/cd-1.md` (the request as the user wrote it, saved at activation). It is already on disk, so no snapshot was needed.
+- No plan exists yet under `.context/`.
+- Repo state at test time: branch `feature/gh-1-pipeline`, base `main`. `Makefile` targets `build` and `stream` exit 1 (not implemented). `transform/models/` holds only `.gitkeep`. `data/raw/` holds the USAspending zips, the USAspending README, the Census CSVs (2021 and 2024 vintages) and `sitematrix.json`. No `lake/` or `out/` yet.
+
+## Scenarios traced
+
+- S1. Fresh checkout, `make build`, then `make build` again. Expect no output change. Result: gap G-13 (write disposition not stated).
+- S2. The stream consumer runs, the connection drops, the consumer reconnects and resumes. Expect no event counted twice and none lost. Result: cannot be judged; gap G-1.
+- S3. `make stream` is stopped and restarted with a different `DURATION`. Expect the same counts as one unbroken run. Result: gaps G-1 and G-2.
+- S4. An event with event time 12:21 arrives when the highest event time seen so far is 12:31. Its window is 12:15 to 12:20; 12:31 is more than 10 minutes after 12:20. The event is late and goes to `late_events`. Result: rule is clear within one run. Cross-run case is G-2.
+- S5. An event with event time 12:30 arrives when the highest seen is 12:30. Its window is 12:25 to 12:30; 12:30 is not more than 10 minutes after 12:30. The event is on time. Result: rule is clear.
+- S6. An edit with no `length.old` or `length.new` (for example a log event). Result: gap G-8.
+- S7. Check 3 on an award whose transactions net to a negative sum in FY2024. Result: gap G-3.
+- S8. A FY2024 award with no state or county (foreign place, multi-county place, or missing FIPS). Check 4 must still hold. Result: gap G-4.
+- S9. A county key in the population source that the 2024 file lacks. Result: gap G-12.
+- S10. The same code is pointed at `https://stream.wikimedia.org/v2/stream/recentchange` for the live demo. The disconnect and resume behaviour may differ from the replay server. Result: gap G-1.
+- S11. Check 6 names `en.wikipedia.org`. The stream carries `wiki` and `server_name`; the sitematrix carries `dbname` and `url`. No join key is named. Result: gap G-10.
+- S12. An analyst runs an oracle check against `out/marts/` only, and the answer lives in the fact table. Result: conflict C-1 and gap G-5.
+
+## Gaps
+
+- G-1 (blocking). No dedupe key and no resume position are named for stream events. The spec requires exact resume with no double count and no loss, and says the replay server disconnects. The candidate key is the recentchange `meta.id`. The resume position (SSE event id or Last-Event-ID, or a stored offset) and where it is persisted are not stated.
+- G-2 (blocking). The lateness watermark is defined as the highest event time among earlier arrivals. The spec does not say whether that maximum persists across `make stream` runs and reconnects, or whether late events raise it. Check 7 and the on-time split in check 6 depend on this.
+- G-3 (blocking). Check 3 counts "awards", but the fact grain is one transaction. The spec does not name the award key (for example `generated_unique_award_id`). It also does not say whether net obligation is summed per award over FY2024 transactions before the sign test.
+- G-4 (blocking). The spec does not say whether place means place of performance or recipient location. It does not say how rows without a state or county are handled. Check 4 (county totals equal state totals, state totals equal the source total) fails or silently drops rows unless an unplaced rule exists.
+- G-5 (blocking). Publication scope is unclear. The spec says downstream reads only `out/marts/`. It does not say whether the star-schema fact and dimension tables are published there. `oracle_map.yml` allows a "table or SQL view", which may point outside `out/marts/`.
+- G-6 (non-blocking). Mart column names and types are not listed. The dbt contracts and `oracle_map.yml` cannot be written from the spec alone.
+- G-7 (non-blocking). The source amount type and the money precision are not stated. "Summed exactly" needs a fixed DECIMAL precision.
+- G-8 (non-blocking). Net bytes with a missing `length.old` or `length.new` is not defined. It is not stated whether such an event counts as an edit with 0 bytes.
+- G-9 (non-blocking). The bot split uses the recentchange `bot` flag. The rule for a missing flag is not stated.
+- G-10 (non-blocking). The wiki key for check 6 is not named. `en.wikipedia.org` must map to the stream `wiki` value (`enwiki`) through the sitematrix.
+- G-11 (non-blocking). "The replayed hour" for check 5 has no start or end. It is not stated whether the hour is taken by event time or arrival time.
+- G-12 (non-blocking). The population fallback says "latest earlier estimate". The join key (state and county FIPS) and the role of the 2021 file are not stated. `co-est2024-alldata.csv` has `POPESTIMATE2024` for all 3144 county rows, so the fallback applies only to keys absent from that file. The 2020 base (`ESTIMATESBASE2020`) must not be read as the population.
+- G-13 (non-blocking). The write disposition for each dlt source is not stated. dlt appends by default. "Running twice must not change any output" needs replace or merge per source.
+- G-14 (non-blocking). Check 2 has no rule for ties or very small populations.
+- G-15 (non-blocking). The stack paragraph has no heading. Output 3 refers to "the stack section" without a name. Minor.
+
+## Conflicts
+
+- C-1. "Anything downstream reads only out/marts/" conflicts with `oracle_map.yml` answering a check with any table or SQL view. Tied to G-5.
+
+## Risks for P1
+
+- The planner must choose a durable stream state store that holds the dedupe key, the resume position and the watermark. Without G-1 and G-2 fixed, no plan step can be verified.
+- The planner must choose the award key and the unplaced rule before writing the check-3 and check-4 queries.
+- Amounts and sums must use DECIMAL, not floats, in the staging models.
+
+## Blocking gaps
+
+G-1: No dedupe key and no resume position for stream events are named, so "no double count, no loss" across reconnects and restarts cannot be checked.
+G-2: The lateness watermark is not stated to persist across `make stream` runs or reconnects, and it is not stated whether late events raise it.
+G-3: The award key for check 3 is not named, and the sum-then-sign rule per award is not stated.
+G-4: The place rule (performance or recipient) and the handling of rows with no state or county are not stated, so check 4 cannot be checked.
+G-5: The publication scope of `out/marts/` is not stated for the star-schema fact and dimension tables, and it conflicts with the oracle map (C-1).
+
+## Verdict
+
+Verdict: NOT READY FOR PLANNING
